<title>INDIA: Indian call money trading closing for holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian call money trading closing for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's call money markets were closed on Wednesday as banks shut for the Mahatma Gandhi birth anniversary holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>They reopen on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, call rates closed at 10.60-75 percent compared to the day's opening of 10.50-10.80 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
